provides turret
suggests gamemaster

import turrets.py
import turret_brains.mast
import turrets.mast
import turret_deploy.mast
# GM placement rides the EXISTING gamemaster spawn menu, so it is a soft dependency:
# without the gamemaster addon these routes simply never fire.
import turret_gm.mast

# TOP LEVEL, and it has to be. The engine reads the extra ship data it has been
# pointed at inside create_new_sim(), so the registration has to happen before the
# first one; declaring inside a label would be too late.
#
# The hulls are a FILE that exists - media/turrets/extraShipData_turrets.yaml, which
# rides the LM media pack - not a file this addon writes. A mastlib is a zip and the
# engine cannot read inside one; a media pack is unpacked to disk once, so the engine
# can simply be handed the folder. Before this, the library accumulated the entries
# and flushed them into the mission's shared extraShipData.json just before
# create_new_sim(), which left a generated file in every mission folder that the
# library then also read back - the same hulls arriving twice.
#
# This is not optional decoration: ENGINE-MEASURED (1.3.5, LM_TestRange test_turret_probe)
# a behav_station fires ONLY from a hull declared this way. Both stock hulls tested stayed
# silent with the identical target_shoot() call; both add-on hulls fired. Without this
# registration every turret in the game is a decorative box.
lm_turret_declare_ships()
